h rates (0%, 2.95%, 5.88% for low/mid/high scenarios). This is not itself a defect. The illustration's 2.1% reduction in growth rate (from 2.9% inflation-adjusted to 0.8%) appears consistent with the RIY statement at low growth. The critical yields (1.9%, 4.8%, 7.8%) represent the breakeven rates needed on the new solution to match the existing solution's projected value, which is a legitimate metric. The 'effect of switching' figures (£10,400, £12,000, £15,000) represent the projected shortfall relative to the existing arrangement at age 75. The cumulative impact is disclosed: the report shows both the RIY impact and the absolute pound value impact, and the illustration demonstrates the effect on fund value from £129,000 to £115,000. The ambiguity arises from whether the 2.1% RIY in the table already includes the 1.00% adviser fee or only the 0.44% product/investment fees. Passage P9 states 'An ongoing annual adviser charge of 1.00% which has been considered as part of the new solution projections below,' suggesting it is included in the comparison. If so, the cumulative impact is properly disclosed. If not, there is an omission.","citations":[{"passageId":"P9","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"An ongoing annual adviser charge of 1.00% which has been considered as part of the new solution projections below.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Reduction in yield [1] - 0.3%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Reduction in yield [1] - 2.1%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Effect of switching - £12,000 or 9.4% decrease","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Illustration - new.md","category":"H","quote":"All charges could reduce this pension fund from £129,000.00 to £115,000.00 - this is the same as reducing the investment growth after inflation from 2.9